It's been said, but it is worth repeating - you really want a ring of
conflict for the Planes and even Astral.  Your pet angel will turn on
you but who cares?  Angels make crappy pets unless you give them buff
armor and level them up over time.  The pet you get on Astral isn't
very useful.

You already have slow digestion, levitation, teleport control, and free
action.  Good.  Put on that free action and keep it.  Getting paralyzed
can happen a lot in the late game and the priests on Astral can
paralyze so you want that ring on all the time.

rings of regen are next to useless in the end run.  I think if you
actually need regeneration you are doing something wrong: you are
fighting too much.

I dont think this has been mentioned.  The spell drain life drains
enchantments.  You *NEVER* need cursed scrolls of enchant armor or
enchant weapon if you can cast drain life.  Just drop the item on the
ground, stand next to it, and zap it with DL.  Its enchantment will
decrease by one (there is no message).  I normally find getting all my
armor to +5 a pain, but not when I have drain life.

Your AC is fine.  Your HP is good, too.  I like to get at least 300 HP
before I ascend and you are over that.  You don't really need a lot of
HP unless you plan on giving Death a big hug, but you can just kill all
the riders with magic missile.  Save your wands of death as back up,
except against Death of course.

Bring as many wands of death, teleportation, and polmorph as you can
get.  Use teleportation to get monsters away.  Polymorph tough
monsters, they will probably turn into something weaker.  Bring wands
of secret door detection to help you find doors in Rodney's tower, the
Sanctum, and to help find portals in the Planes (especially the Plane
of Water).

There is no limit to the amount of HP and POW you can get.  Nurse
dancing, playing with succubi/incubi, potions of gain level, wraith
corpses, and alchemy will always increase these stats.

Though I'm not a big fan of nurse dancing because it involves taking
off your armor and leaves you vulnerable to all sorts of attacks.

On Astral, the spell of charm monster is like an I WIN button.  If you
get surrounded, cast charm monster and watch your enemies turn into
friends.  It gets even better if you have a magic whistle.  Just try
not to kill any pets with a stray ray of death.  Your god won't like
that.

Jumping is also a great spell on Astral.  Use a wand of teleport to
clear some room and then jump.  You will get to the altar that much
faster using this method.

You don't *need* cure sickness, but it is nice.  It's too bad your
chaotic because Holy Water cures sickness for Lawfuls and Neutrals.



